  "notes": "Source: University of Arkansas East Arkansas Community College (UA-EACC) official program page 'Associate of Applied Science in Nursing - LPN/LPTN-RN Accelerated Track' (dated 8/7/2025), verified in-session. Unusual structure, modeled honestly: (1) the page lists 23 credits of General Education as 'Required before admission to the LPN/LPTN Accelerated Track' with no term assignment, so those 7 courses are recorded as external_prereqs, not sequenced; (2) the track itself is sequenced as Term III (Summer) / Term IV (Fall) / Term V (Spring) because entrants hold LPN/LPTN licensure covering Terms I-II; (3) the page's stated 'Total Degree Credit Hours 62' = 23 pre-admission + 35 sequenced here + 4 escrow credits for previous LPN learning held after successful completion of NUR 1904 ('NURSING CREDITS FOR PREVIOUS LEARNING'); total_credits is therefore the sequenced sum 35 (11+14+10). Six 0-credit clinical-application courses are genuine requirements (required_zero). Term IV social-science slot: 'SOC 1013 Introduction to Sociology OR SOC 2043 Anthropology' rendered as a choice with code = first-listed option. Page lists both NUR 2134 and NUR 2254 under the title 'Medical Surgical Nursing II' (the NUR 2250 clinical is titled '...Medical Surgical Nursing III'); titles copied verbatim. Graduates may apply for the NCLEX-RN. program_type 'accelerated': official page titles this the 'LPN/LPTN-RN Accelerated Track'; 23 cr gen-ed required before admission.",
